  "contract_review": {
    "scale": "X0=(shortScale bs:Real), the unchanged product of all original block lower endpoints, equal to original MUV by previous theorem. Independent of tuple,m,q,rho,xi.",
    "actual_input": "Same actual scalarProfile nonzero at completeProduct ns, j in range 3, ns in original rectangle, fixed distinct i/k, and literal original Dictionary short-position condition. No desired M/support/error bound or aggregate nonzero is a final premise.",
    "chart_window": "Extract original psi nonzero from scalarProfile; apply old profile_nonzero_support via original tupleProfile singleton. With prior all-rectangle product window this gives R<=128 X0 and X0<=2 R.",
    "short_product": "Original short cardinality<=4 and lower<R^(3 zeta) give M<=R^(12 zeta) using finite product monotonicity. The positive gap 28 zeta absorbs 128^(12 zeta) at fixed X0, yielding M<=X0^(40 zeta).",
    "short_slots": "A separate positive 1-3 zeta gap absorbs 2*128^(3 zeta), yielding 2 lower<=X0 for every original short position.",
    "roughness": "Original beforeHBCutoff K [cj] is roughF(v), v=2^(6K+2)*(2R). True geometry gives X0<=v<=256*2^(6K+2)*X0. After K is fixed, X0 large gives v<=X0^2. Original arbitrary-v roughF_mono/upper are applied, never the old factor16 helper.",
